@startuml stepup-sequence
' MCP mid-interaction per-operation authorization with RAR remediation
' (RFC 9396 + draft-ietf-oauth-rar-metadata-remediation), matching mcp-stepup-lab:
' TS SDK 1.32, node-oidc-provider 9.12

!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
skinparam sequenceBoxBorderColor #999999
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #666666
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EEF2F7
autonumber "<b>[00]"

title MCP mid-interaction authorization: 401 insufficient_authorization + RAR remediation + one-shot token\n(pre-authorization elicitation, pending operation, session token preserved)

actor "User" as U
participant "User Agent\n(browser)" as UA

box "Agent" #F3F7FF
  participant "LLM loop\n(Claude)" as LLM
  participant "MCP Client\n(SDK transport +\nstepUpFetch / OAuthSession)" as C
end box

box "MCP Server (Resource Server)" #F4FBF4
  participant "HTTP layer\n(auth + challenge rewrite)" as RS
  participant "Tool handler\n(transfer)" as T
  database "Pending-op store\n+ consumed jti" as OPS
end box

participant "AS\n(node-oidc-provider,\nRAR enabled)" as AS

== 0. Bootstrap: SESSION token (scope=mcp:basic) ==

C -> RS : POST /mcp initialize (no Authorization)
RS --> C : **401** WWW-Authenticate: Bearer scope="mcp:basic",\n  resource_metadata="http://mcp-server:3000/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp"
note right of C : stepUpFetch HOLDS the request
C -> RS : GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp
RS --> C : PRM {resource, authorization_servers:[iss], scopes_supported:["mcp:basic"]}
C -> AS : GET {iss}/.well-known/openid-configuration (back-channel)
AS --> C : AS metadata: authorization/token endpoints,\nauthorization_details_types_supported:["money_transfer"],\nauthorization_details_types_metadata_endpoint
C -> U : "Open this URL": /auth?scope=mcp:basic&resource=…&code_challenge=…
U -> UA : open URL
UA -> AS : GET /auth
AS --> UA : login page
U -> UA : alice / ****
UA -> AS : POST /interaction/{uid}/login
AS --> UA : consent "Read your accounts and balances (mcp:basic)"
U -> UA : Allow
AS --> UA : 302 redirect_uri?code&state
UA -> C : GET http://localhost:8765/callback?code&state
C -> AS : POST /token (code, code_verifier, resource)
AS --> C : **T1** JWT (aud=MCP resource, scope="mcp:basic", 600 s)
C -> C : store T1 as the SESSION token
C -> RS : **replay** POST initialize (Bearer T1)
RS --> C : 200 + Mcp-Session-Id: S (session bound to sub)
C -> RS : POST notifications/initialized → 202
C -> RS : GET /mcp (standalone SSE stream, Bearer T1)
RS --> C : 200 text/event-stream (kept open; carries the elicitation later)

U -> LLM : "what are my balances?"
LLM -> C : tool_use get_accounts
C -> RS : POST tools/call get_accounts [Bearer T1]
RS --> C : 200 balances

== 1. Transfer: the tool discovers it needs a per-operation grant ==

U -> LLM : "send R$ 800 to carol@pix.example from checking"
LLM -> C : tool_use transfer{from_account, pix_key, amount}
C -> RS : POST /mcp tools/call transfer [JSON-RPC id=7, Mcp-Session-Id=S, Bearer T1]
RS -> RS : verify T1 (sig, iss, aud); session token (mcp:basic); sub == session sub
RS -> T : dispatch in per-request context (JSON response mode: no status line yet)
T -> OPS : findByRequest(S, 7)
OPS --> T : none
T -> T : validate account + balance (read-only)
T -> T : detail = {type:"money_transfer",\n  debtor_account:{account_id:"checking"},\n  creditor_account:{pix_key:"carol@pix.example"},\n  instructed_amount:{currency:"BRL", amount:"800.00"}}
T -> OPS : createOperation(op_X, key=(S,7), argsHash, checkpoint{detail})\nstatus = awaiting_confirmation

== 2. Pre-authorization elicitation (UX only) ==

T -> RS : elicitation/create (form), no relatedRequestId
RS -->> C : SSE (GET stream): "Pending payment op_X: R$ 800.00 checking → carol… Continue?"
C -> U : terminal prompt [Y/n/c]
alt user declines
  U -> C : n
  C -> RS : POST JSON-RPC result {action:"accept", content:{proceed:false}} → 202
  T -> OPS : status = cancelled
  RS --> C : **200** result "op_X cancelled, nothing executed" [id=7]  (no 401, no browser)
  C --> LLM : tool_result
else user proceeds
  U -> C : y
  C -> RS : POST JSON-RPC result {action:"accept", content:{proceed:true}} → 202
  T -> OPS : status = awaiting_authorization
end

== 3. Challenge: insufficient_authorization with remediation (atomic) ==

T -> T : requireAuthorizationDetails(detail)\nT1 has no matching authorization_details → missing\nguard: committed[] empty → challenge allowed
T -> RS : record challenge; abort tool
note right of RS : The SDK's isError result is discarded and rewritten.\nRule: 4xx ⇒ nothing executed for this request.
RS --> C : **401 Unauthorized**\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_authorization",\n  error_description="Additional authorization is required: money_transfer … [operation op_X]",\n  authorization_remediation=base64url({"authorization_details":[detail]}),\n  resource_metadata="…/oauth-protected-resource/mcp"\n(no authorization_reference: tokens are single-use)\nbody (non-normative): JSON-RPC error {id:7, code:-32001, data:{authorization_remediation, operation_id}}

== 4. Client remediation: ONE-SHOT token (request id=7 HELD, LLM unaware) ==

C -> C : decode authorization_remediation → authorization_details\nno authorization_reference ⇒ nothing cached to retry with (§7.1 step 2)
C -> RS : GET PRM (resource_metadata)
RS --> C : PRM → AS
C -> C : check "money_transfer" ∈ authorization_details_types_supported\nnew PKCE + state\n**no scope parameter** (do not re-request existing permissions)
C -> U : "Open this URL": /auth?authorization_details=[detail]&resource=…&code_challenge=…
U -> UA : open URL
UA -> AS : GET /auth
AS -> AS : validate money_transfer against its schema\nSSO session → no login; RAR present → consent required
AS --> UA : consent "Approve this payment: R$ 800.00 · from checking · to carol@pix.example · one-time"
alt user denies
  U -> UA : Deny
  AS --> UA : 302 redirect_uri?error=access_denied
  UA -> C : GET /callback?error=access_denied
  C --> LLM : original 401 surfaced → tool call fails
  note over T, OPS : op_X stays awaiting_authorization until TTL → failed.\nNothing committed. T1 still valid.
else user approves
  U -> UA : Approve payment
  AS --> UA : 302 redirect_uri?code&state
  UA -> C : GET /callback?code&state
  C -> AS : POST /token (code, code_verifier, resource)
  AS --> C : **T2** JWT (aud=MCP resource, **no scope**,\nauthorization_details:[detail], 120 s, no refresh token)
  note right of C : T2 is NOT stored. T1 remains the session token.

  == 5. Replay with T2, resume from checkpoint, burn T2 ==

  C -> RS : **replay** POST tools/call transfer [same id=7, same S, same body, Bearer T2]
  RS -> RS : verify T2; one-shot token (details only) → allowed ONLY for a payment tools/call;\nsub(T2) == session sub
  RS -> T : dispatch
  T -> OPS : findByRequest(S, 7)
  OPS --> T : op_X (awaiting_authorization)
  T -> T : sub + argsHash match → SKIP validation/elicitation (checkpoint)
  T -> OPS : jti(T2) consumed?
  OPS --> T : no
  T -> T : requireAuthorizationDetails(detail): T2 details == detail → OK
  T -> T : re-validate balance; commit("transfer op_X") **(only side effect)**
  T -> OPS : consume jti(T2); op_X = completed + stored result
  RS --> C : **200** result "Transfer done (operation op_X)" [id=7]
  C -> C : discard T2
  C --> LLM : tool_result (401/elicitation/browser hops invisible to the LLM)
  LLM --> U : "Done: R$ 800 sent to carol@pix.example"
end

== 6. Later calls keep using the SESSION token ==

U -> LLM : "what are my balances now?"
LLM -> C : tool_use get_accounts
C -> RS : POST tools/call get_accounts [Bearer **T1**]
RS --> C : 200 balances (no login, no consent)

== 7. Idempotent duplicate replay (lost response / retry) ==

C -> RS : POST tools/call transfer [id=7, S, Bearer T2] (again)
RS -> T : dispatch
T -> OPS : findByRequest(S, 7) → op_X completed
T --> RS : stored result (no re-execution, no second debit)
RS --> C : 200 same result

== 8. A one-shot token cannot be reused ==

C -> RS : POST tools/call get_accounts [Bearer T2]
RS --> C : **403** Bearer error="insufficient_scope", scope="mcp:basic"\n("one-shot operation token can only be used for the operation it authorizes")
C -> RS : POST tools/call transfer (identical payment, NEW id=9) [Bearer T2]
RS -> T : dispatch → new op_Y
T -> OPS : jti(T2) consumed? → yes
RS --> C : **401** insufficient_authorization + remediation for op_Y
ref over C, UA, AS : phases 4–5 again: a fresh one-shot token for op_Y

== 9. Guard: challenge after a side effect (non-atomic tool) ==

LLM -> C : tool_use naive_batch_transfer{[R$ 20 → zed (new payee)]}
C -> RS : POST tools/call [id=10, Bearer T1]
RS -> T : dispatch
T -> T : register payee zed → commit (committed[] = [payee])
T -> T : requireAuthorizationDetails([…]) → missing
T -> T : **guard**: committed[] not empty → ChallengeAfterCommit\n(no 401: it would claim "nothing happened")
RS --> C : **200** isError "Partially executed: payee registered; no transfer executed"
C --> LLM : tool_result (in-band partial progress)
note over C, AS : With known payees nothing is committed first: one 401 carries N authorization_details,\nso one consent and one one-shot token cover the whole batch.

legend bottom left
  <b>Key properties</b>
  • Tools never advertise the requirement; it is discovered during execution.
  • Remediation follows draft-ietf-oauth-rar-metadata-remediation: 401, error="insufficient_authorization",
    authorization_remediation = base64url({authorization_details}); no authorization_reference (single use).
  • Operation token: authorization_details only, NO scope, short TTL, no refresh, burned by jti at commit.
  • Session token (mcp:basic) is never replaced; it keeps serving every other request.
  • Elicitation is UX (intent + "something is in course"), never the authorization itself.
  • Atomic challenge: allowed only while nothing has been committed in the request.
  • (Mcp-Session-Id, JSON-RPC id) identifies the pending operation across the replay.
  • Requires JSON response mode; the client raises the request timeout (5 min) for held requests.
endlegend

@enduml
